@startuml seq-share
!theme plain
autonumber

actor "Visitor" as V
participant "Browser\n(site loader JS)" as B
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "Analytics Collector" as COL
queue "Kafka" as K
participant "Social platform" as SOC
participant "CDN" as CDN

V -> B : click "Share" on the portfolio
B -> B : show the share sheet with the canonical page address
V -> B : choose a platform, for example Behance
B -> SOC : open the platform's share page\nwith the canonical page address

B -> GW : POST /events (beacon)\n{portfolioId, eventType = SHARE, platform}
GW -> COL : forward
COL -> COL : validate, compute visitorHash
COL ->> K : analytics.events, key = eventId
COL --> GW : 202 Accepted

note over SOC
  Later, the platform's crawler fetches the page
  to build the preview card for the post.
end note
SOC -> CDN : GET /{slug}
CDN --> SOC : HTML with og:title, og:description\nand og:image = /media/{mediaId}/og-1200.jpg
SOC -> CDN : GET /media/{mediaId}/og-1200.jpg
CDN --> SOC : 1200 px JPEG
note over SOC
  The OG_1200 variant is generated once by the
  Media Worker, so every platform gets a
  correctly sized image.
end note
@enduml
